[{"id":"marker0","name":"Hienion Volcano","legend":"Erupting volcano. Height: 2704m."},{"id":"marker1","name":"Hot Springs of Shahr","legend":"A geothermal springs with naturally heated water that provide relaxation and medicinal benefits. Average temperature is 20°C."},{"id":"marker2","name":"Vogtstetten Hot Springs","legend":"A geothermal springs with naturally heated water that provide relaxation and medicinal benefits. Average temperature is 49°C."},{"id":"marker3","name":"Sachringen Enchanted Reservoir","legend":"This legendary water source is whispered about in ancient tales and believed to possess mystical properties. The spring emanates crystal-clear water, shimmering with an otherworldly iridescence that sparkles even in the dimmest light."},{"id":"marker4","name":"Bagold — lead mining town","legend":"Bagold is a mining town of 1081 people just nearby the lead mine."},{"id":"marker5","name":"Steiburg — silver mining town","legend":"Steiburg is a mining town of 4621 people just nearby the silver mine."},{"id":"marker6","name":"Baghstan — gold mining town","legend":"Baghstan is a mining town of 841 people just nearby the gold mine."},{"id":"marker7","name":"Rampidu — gold mining town","legend":"Rampidu is a mining town of 1494 people just nearby the gold mine."},{"id":"marker8","name":"Olbia — salt mining town","legend":"Olbia is a mining town of 886 people just nearby the salt mine."},{"id":"marker9","name":"Sidea — iron mining town","legend":"Sidea is a mining town of 1674 people just nearby the iron mine."},{"id":"marker10","name":"Isitura Bridge","legend":"An old crossing of the Medunaka River, rarely used since being rumoured to attract trolls."},{"id":"marker11","name":"Druvorum Bridge","legend":"A stone bridge spans over the Aupica River near Druvorum."},{"id":"marker12","name":"The Huge Ox","legend":"A big and famous roadside inn. Delicious fried chickpea with white cider is served here."},{"id":"marker13","name":"The Fat Inn","legend":"A big and famo