 afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker76","name":"Khvordishan Monster","legend":"Legends say a relic monster of 5 m long inhabits Khvordishan Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker77","name":"Haford Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 16 m long."},{"id":"marker78","name":"Helston Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 12 m long."},{"id":"marker79","name":"Newen Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 33 m long."},{"id":"marker80","name":"Lintongay Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 15 m long."},{"id":"marker81","name":"Ruvate Cyclops","legend":"Tales speak of a terrifying Cyclops who inhabits Ruvate hills and prefers eating children."},{"id":"marker82","name":"Baghshak Warg","legend":"Whispers speak of a big Warg who inhabits Baghshak hills and terrorizes the region."},{"id":"marker83","name":"Lentiateson Bearded Devil","legend":"Whispers speak of a lucky Bearded Devil who inhabits Lentiateson hills and snatches people from homes."},{"id":"marker84","name":"Mheabermo Bearded Devil","legend":"Tipplers speak of a prime Bearded Devil who inhabits Mheabermo hills and terrorizes the region."},{"id":"marker85","name":"Brinver Giant","legend":"Elders speak of a superior Giant who inhabits Brinver hills and terrorizes the region."},{"id":"marker86","name":"Hepehatom Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Ahedstan Religion."},{"id":"marker87","name":"Hariziche Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Ahedstan Religion."},{"id":"marker88","name":"Meza Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Linnocobris Faith."},{"id":"marker89","name":"Ruladshad Forest","legend":"A forest sacred 